# requirements-linux-py314.in: what requirements-linux-py314.lock holds
# beyond pyproject.toml's dependencies and its real-clients and
# voice-profile extras, which the lock compiles from pyproject.toml itself.
#
# The lock is the production install of a Linux server: CPython 3.14,
# x86_64, CPU-only torch from the PyTorch CPU index, every package at an
# exact version with its SHA-256s (docs/LINUX_HOST.md, "Install";
# scripts/linux/apply-update.sh, sync_deps). Regenerate it with
# scripts/linux/compile-linux-lock.sh, which runs pip-compile in a pinned
# python:3.14-slim container so the resolver sees Linux and Python 3.14
# whatever machine you run it on, and commit the files together: this one,
# the lock, and requirements-linux-py314-no-deps.lock (written beside it).

# The speaker encoder's weights (resemblyzer) and faster-whisper are not
# here: they are installed without their declared dependencies, from
# requirements-linux-py314-no-deps.lock, which compile-linux-lock.sh writes
# from requirements-no-deps.in (PyAV, librosa, soxr, soundfile: LGPL
# libraries Domovoi doesn't use).

# The bundled radio plugin's fingerprinter (pyproject's fingerprint extra:
# numpy and scipy). librosa brought scipy until 2026-10-15; listed here so
# a Linux server keeps fingerprinting radio samples.
scipy>=1.11

# The build backend: of this project (pip install --no-deps -e .) and of the
# few pins that publish only an sdist. The install builds them with
# --no-build-isolation against this hash-checked copy, so no build step
# downloads an unchecked setuptools of its own. Below 82: webrtcvad, which
# imports pkg_resources (gone in setuptools 82), was built this way until
# 2026-10-15; the bound stays until a lock is tested with 82.
setuptools>=68,<82
wheel>=0.43
